    {
      "short_id": "short266",
      "angle": "The final notice threatened termination but omitted the place, hours, and decision-maker available for disputing a bill.",
      "avoids": "No claim of overbilling; no unqualified adoption of the record's conflicting account; no claim that a hearing prevents all shutoffs.",
      "funnel_question_left_for_longform": "The Court did not abolish shutoffs, so what procedural protection did it actually add?",
      "loop": true,
      "loop_join": "The final line returns to the sparse notice from the first frame.",
      "era": "Memphis, Tennessee, 1970s",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "L1",
          "text": "The final notice said payment was overdue and service would stop unless money arrived by a date. That was the whole warning.",
          "delivery": "intense",
          "source_lines": [
            "Pay or face termination."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L2",
          "text": "It did not tell the recipient that a billing dispute might be discussed with company representatives before the service stopped.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Whatever else this case is, it is not a case about a utility that offered nothing."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L3",
          "text": "The omission mattered because a phone line, employees, credit counselors, and payment arrangements existed elsewhere in the system.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "These employees also direct callers to credit counselors who are authorized to resolve disputes on a more permanent basis and who can set up extended payment plans for customers in financial difficulty."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L4",
          "text": "But lower courts found that the relevant procedure had not been adequately explained or made available to Mary Craft when she sought help.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "She was given no satisfaction."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L5",
          "text": "The Supreme Court said a sufficient cutoff notice should state where, during which hours, and before whom a disputed bill could be considered.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "And the Court said what a sufficient notice would contain."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L6",
          "text": "That holding changed the information supplied before termination. It did not decide whether the Crafts owed the disputed amount.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Nobody ever decided whether the Crafts owed the money."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L7",
          "text": "It also did not eliminate termination: after notice and an opportunity to be heard, the utility could still cut service if the bill was justly due.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "And petitioners would retain the option to terminate service after affording this opportunity and concluding that the amount billed was justly due."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L8",
          "text": "The defect was therefore visible on the page itself: a deadline and a threat, with the path to a human decision-maker left blank.",
          "delivery": "calm",
          "source_lines": [
            "The MLG&W notice only warned the customer to pay or face termination."
          ],
          "claims": []
        }
      ],
